description:
File: packages/swf/src/sprite.ts

Bug: When a TextDisplayObject with antiAlias='readability' or antiAlias='custom' (CSM) is defined inside a symbol timeline, sprite.ts emits DefineEditText (tag 37) for the text but NEVER emits CSMTextSettings (tag 74) immediately after. This causes FlashType-quality anti-aliasing to be unavailable for all text placed inside movie clips, buttons, or graphic symbols.

compile.ts handles this correctly: after emitting DefineEditText (lines 1227-1228), it checks obj.antiAlias and conditionally emits encodeCSMTextSettings (lines 1234-1241):
  if (aa === 'readability') { csmBody = encodeCSMTextSettings(charId, 0, 0); writer.writeTag(...) }
  else if (aa === 'custom' && obj.csm) { csmBody = encodeCSMTextSettings(charId, obj.csm.thickness, obj.csm.sharpness); ... }

In sprite.ts the text character pre-pass (lines 132-138) calls encodeDefineEditText() and pushes to hoistedDefs — but there is no check for antiAlias and no CSMTextSettings is appended to hoistedDefs.

Fix prescription:
In sprite.ts lines 132-138 (the hoistedDefs.push for text objects), after computing the DefineEditText body and pushing it, add:
  const aa = obj.antiAlias;
  if (aa === 'readability') {
    hoistedDefs.push({ tagType: Tag.CSMTextSettings, body: encodeCSMTextSettings(charId, 0, 0) });
  } else if (aa === 'custom' && obj.csm) {
    hoistedDefs.push({ tagType: Tag.CSMTextSettings, body: encodeCSMTextSettings(charId, obj.csm.thickness, obj.csm.sharpness) });
  }

Also add the import of encodeCSMTextSettings from './text.js' (currently only encodeDefineEditText and encodePlaceObject2ForText are imported at line 35).

Tag.CSMTextSettings is already defined in tags.ts (74).

Acceptance test: symbol with a text field with antiAlias='readability'; after encodeDefineSprite, assert that hoistedDefs includes a tag-74 (CSMTextSettings) entry immediately following the tag-37 (DefineEditText) entry for that text character ID.
